# Keep the build context small and keep secrets out of it.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
coverage
**/coverage
.git
.github
*.log
# A bare `.env` pattern matches the context ROOT only, so `apps/api/.env` —
# which is where the development secrets actually live — was reaching the
# build stage. Verified with `docker build --output type=local`: without the
# `**/` forms, apps/api/.env lands in the image build. The negations must be
# doubled up the same way, or .env.example gets excluded with the rest.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
.storage
.storage-test
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.venv
**/.venv
.pytest_cache
services/ai/artifacts
services/ai/data
# The frontend. Deployed by Vercel from apps/web, never built by Docker --
# neither Dockerfile COPYs it. In a single repository serving both targets it
# would otherwise be uploaded into the backend build context on every Render
# deploy for nothing.
apps/web
docs
*.md
!README.md
